"fix(dependencies): pin integrity reads to file handles\n\n## Problem\n\nThe first full main-branch CodeQL scan reported two high-severity `js/file-system-race` findings in official release verification and supply-chain fingerprints: [alert 1](https://github.com/Cirnouo/debugging-cdp-targets/security/code-scanning/1) and [alert 2](https://github.com/Cirnouo/debugging-cdp-targets/security/code-scanning/2). Both checked file metadata before reopening the pathname to read its contents. A deterministic filesystem test demonstrated that replacing that path after inspection allowed the replacement bytes to be read.\n\n## Resulting behavior\n\nBoth integrity checks now use a shared regular-file reader that opens once, checks the descriptor, and reads through that same descriptor. It compares path/device/inode evidence and observed size/modification/change-time metadata around the read, rejects observed replacement or mutation, and closes the descriptor on every outcome. Unix also uses no-follow and nonblocking open flags; Windows retains descriptor/path checks where those flags are unavailable.\n\nCanonical package-root checks, complete release inventory, digest verification, fingerprint framing, exact dependency versions, original upstream release bytes and both dependency locks remain unchanged. The maintained gateway and standalone security checker are regenerated from source.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Regression tests observed the path-replacement and in-place-mutation failures before implementation, then passed with the fix.\n- `node --test tests/file-evidence.test.ts tests/official-package.test.ts tests/supply-chain.test.ts`: 34/34 passed, including descriptor cleanup after inspection/read failures and existing package-link rejection.\n- [x] Focused tests and `pnpm verify:push` pass (278/278 regression tests).\n- [x] `pnpm check:security` passed: repository signatures 169/169 and upstream signatures 16/16; no reported, waived or blocked vulnerabilities.\n- [x] Runtime source changes include regenerated gateway and standalone auditor output, with reproducible-build and distribution checks.\n\nHosted CI and CodeQL results are required before merge, including both real Chrome acceptance jobs and positive extraction evidence for the native C# helper. The main-branch scan after merge must confirm both existing alerts are fixed.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [x] Supply-chain policy, source/test/tooling indexes and meaningful Unreleased security changes are updated.\n- [x] The PR title and commit follow the repository policy.\n- [x] Version 0.1.0 remains unreleased."
